 driven  narratives all set against a billboard  sized converse and led by a near  supernatural sense of fate which is  barely even glimpsed in his earlier  works the result is a colorful mosaic of  a movie that proved to be one of 1999's  most challenging and rewarding releases  of all the fantastic movies released in  1999 few had quite the cultural impact  enjoyed by a night Shyamalan  spellbinding supernatural thriller The  Sixth Sense Shyamalan s masterpiece  arrived in theaters under a shroud of  mystery but thanks to a star turned from  Bruce Willis one of the greatest child  performances in history from Haley Joel  Osment and the mind-blowing twist ending  it became a legitimate cultural  phenomenon almost overnight it also  cleared well north of half a billion  dollars at the box office  earned a six Academy Award nominations  and made a household name of the man who  wrote and directed it over the years  Hollywood and Shyamalan himself has  repeatedly tried and mostly failed to  reproduce a bracing impact of the film's  twisty narrative because Shyamalan  vision is so skillfully executed and  vividly realized a sixth sense has only  grown in esteem as a result and the  film's hefty emotional impact still hits  home whether you know its secrets or not  in fact part of the fun of you watching  The Sixth Sense is searching for clues  that you missed the first three or four  or even five times through but what's  overshadowed by the film's twist is that  at its core the sixth sense is also a  tenderly observed drama about grief and  loss fronted by a troubled youth  learning to accept the burdens of a gift  he never asked for that Shyamalan fitted  such high drama into a genuinely  unsettling ghost story is what  makes a sixth sense the stuff of genre  legend just a week prior to the Six  Senses arrival in theaters another  stunning supernatural confection hit  theaters in the form of The Blair Witch  Project conceived and directed by  newcomers Daniel Myrick 